- op: discuss  # 5f2b
  at: '2026-05-01T19:37:45Z'  # 5f2b
  by: agent  # 5f2b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5f2b
  clock: 2  # 5f2b
  nonce: 5f2b  # 5f2b
  message: "AUDIT VERDICT: DEPRECATE — full ADR-0023-shape migration warranted. Filing follow-on ADR draft as a separate item (this audit's decision artifact is the cluster taxonomy + four-test verdicts below; the ADR is the next-stage deliverable).\n\nINVENTORY: 192 distinct Symbol.kind values found in production code (lowercase identifier-shaped string literals at kind= sites under packages/, excluding tests).\n\nCLUSTER TAXONOMY (the suspect axes, named):\n\nCLUSTER A — Pure language constructs (the canonical, ADR-0023-axis-compliant set; ~30 values): function, class, method, struct, interface, enum, module, variable, property, constructor, namespace, attribute, field, trait, type, type_alias, alias, macro, fn, var, proc, procedure, subroutine, getter, setter, mixin, record, union, typedef, simple_type, defined_type, abstract, const, constant, instance.\n\nCLUSTER B — File-shape entities (~12 values): file, library, dependency, package, executable, program, project, module_file, component_file, npm_package, composer_package, main_entry, bin, binary, library_export, export_entry, wasm_module, tsconfig.\n\nCLUSTER C — Apex/peer overloads (Test 2 fires): function vs fn (apex/peer); variable vs var; procedure vs proc; struct vs structure; (call as apex of \\*_call peers — see Cluster E).\n\nCLUSTER D — Framework roles / dispatch participation (Test 4 fires; analogous to ADR-0023's endpoint_shape values for Edge.edge_type; ~25 values): event_publisher, event_subscriber, ipc_publisher, ipc_caller, ipc_bridge_caller, objc_bridge, crypto_producer, crypto_consumer, message_sender, message_handler, mq_publisher, grpc_service, grpc_servicer, grpc_stub, grpc_server, websocket_endpoint, dispatcher, graphql_resolver, http_client, graphql_client, route_mount, route, route_include, openapi_operation, abi_call, selector_ref. These values encode the symbol's PARTICIPATION in a framework pattern, not what the symbol IS — same axis confusion ADR-0023 identified for Edge.edge_type.\n\nCLUSTER E — Edge labels masquerading as Symbol kinds (Test 3 fires; ~10 values): call, function_call, subprocess_call, db_query, abi_call, import, inherit, reference, write, read, include, extends, route_mount. These name relationships, not symbol categories.\n\nCLUSTER F — Component/UI references (overlaps with Edge.edge_type imports_component fold; ~6 values): component, component_ref, component_file, slot, prop, view.\n\nCLUSTER G — Build/config-shape (~10 values): test, work_item, target, recipe, env_var, build_arg, exposed_port, stage, requirement, editable, url_requirement, setting, config, derivation.\n\nCLUSTER H — Domain-specific (graph / DB / template / config / etc.; the long tail; ~70+ values): section, paragraph, code_block, diagram, plot, yield, for_loop, conditional, declaration, prefix, base, query, entry, task, python_task, addtask, entity, architecture, error_set, participant, state, model, fragment, partial, provider, local, style_block, permission, keyframes, media, font_face, class_selector, id_selector, filter, workflow, subdirectory, workspace, table_array, link, pattern_rule, special_target, table, label, command, environment, binding, varying, id, storage, private, workgroup, source, port, uniform, output, input, value, pattern, handler, subscript, signal, ...\n\nFOUR LEAKAGE TESTS (cluster-level):\n\n- Test 1 (Property derivability): Cluster D values are ALL derivable from edge_type + dst.kind queries (per ADR-0023's pattern). 'event_publisher' = symbol with outgoing event_publishes edge. 'graphql_resolver' = method on a resolver class. 'route_mount' = symbol with outgoing dispatches_to + dispatch_kind=route. **MASSIVE LEAKAGE in Cluster D.**\n\n- Test 2 (Apex/peer overloading): Cluster C explicitly. function/fn, variable/var, procedure/proc — same string playing both 'top type' AND 'short alias' role. **FIRES.**\n\n- Test 3 (Construct vs relationship): Cluster E values are RELATIONSHIPS, not symbol categories. 'call' is what an Edge does, not what a Symbol IS. Putting both in Symbol.kind forces consumers to guess which question they're asking. **FIRES.**\n\n- Test 4 (Mechanism vs category): Cluster D again — \\*_publisher/\\*_subscriber/\\*_caller/\\*_consumer suffixes encode mechanism (HOW a symbol participates in a pattern), not category (WHAT it is). Already flagged by ADR-0023 Open Question #6. **FIRES.**\n\nFOLLOW-ON ADR SCOPE (recommend filing as the next-stage tracker item):\n\nThe migration mirrors ADR-0023's Edge.edge_type playbook, instantiating ADR-0024's axis-declaration template:\n\n1. CANONICAL AXIS: 'language construct' — the value names the source-language syntactic kind. Cluster A is the seed.\n2. DEPRECATION CANDIDATES: Cluster D + Cluster E. Cluster D values fold to Cluster A kinds + meta keys (e.g., event_publisher → method/function + meta['framework_role']='event_publisher'). Cluster E values fold by recognizing they're edge-type confusions: a symbol with kind='call' should have kind='function_call_site' (a call SITE, not a function being defined) OR be eliminated as a duplicate of an Edge.\n3. DOCUMENT-OR-RECLASSIFY: Cluster B (file-shape; arguably a separate axis), Cluster F (UI components — cleanly ADR-0023-Phase-3-shape: component_ref → reference + dst.kind=component already lives in the Edge migration playbook), Cluster G (build/config — separate axis candidate), Cluster H (long tail; per-pair audit needed).\n4. PHASES (per ADR-0023 model):\n   - Phase 1: registry + drift linter (axis_drift.find_drift parameterized to symbol_kind / SYMBOL_KIND name filter — already supported per WI-pilam-jukus generalization)\n   - Phase 2: consumer migration to (kind, edge_type, meta) queries\n   - Phase 3: producer migration (rename Cluster D + Cluster E emit sites)\n   - Phase 4a/4b: schema bump + deprecation removal\n\n5. ESTIMATED BLAST RADIUS: Cluster D has ~25 values, each likely emitted by 1-3 producer linkers and consumed by 0-2 hardcoded sets. Cluster E has ~10 values, more diffusely scattered. Total emit-site count ~50-70 producers across ~30-40 files. Consumer-side enumerations likely <10 (centrality weight tables, slice filters, sketch selection). This is roughly the same scale as ADR-0023 Phase 3 was; expect similar wall-clock time.\n\nFOLLOW-UP: filing WI-(new) for the ADR draft. The audit's decision artifact (this discussion entry) is the input to that ADR's §1 (Context) and §3 (Detailed analysis); §6 (Migration plan) instantiates the four-phase pattern above."  # 5f2b
